 "path": "memory/continual_arc_edge_continuation.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC: incomplete stripe continuation

A demonstrated pattern: a full-width row of a marker color (demo: color 3) serves as the reference stripe. Another row contains the same stripe only in the left portion, with background cells to its right; replace only the missing suffix cells with color 1. Preserve the existing marker cells and all other cells. The test showed this still applies when the row's background is color 6 and the incomplete marker row occurs above a full marker row (demo background was 9 and the partial row below the full row). In the test, extend the 4-cell 9 stripe across columns 4–7 with 1s; all other cells remain unchanged.

Use demos to confirm which partial stripe is missing continuation and which suffix cells are affected; do not assume arbitrary background suffixes should be filled."
